", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"46c4d902db10ba5b32d81e809a5470054eb62d649f2fab637073d296b7aa434e","event_uuid":"7b217d0a-9381-4606-a419-c68c7cf3cb79","position":{"commit_sha":"f9e60dd62b9ed12e55cde4dc291971852314785e","position":"1789902525337100232-7b217d0a-9381-4606-a419-c68c7cf3cb79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"52378004ea9d8263f571e128c7d2d93b1465437cbdc08230ec45051fb2c6b0de","event_uuid":"10f323a9-d314-49e2-adbf-5bea3aed5666","position":{"commit_sha":"070f04bc44104003fd76684985c1eb70d2a08716","position":"1789902633238941379-10f323a9-d314-49e2-adbf-5bea3aed5666"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d087b355d94ff17d77c5a5ed141f0dcd58aa256e554dd75ae313dbd7dc19ddfc","event_uuid":"4e49b572-4b0b-4912-8048-a3ef2d9ec768","position":{"commit_sha":"b98ca002908691f3bbdbdaccb9500e6a9f5a59c5","position":"1789902808184843825-4e49b572-4b0b-4912-8048-a3ef2d9ec768"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c5cb97dd83bd83d1b8779463548003f7bf59ab95bb7f28af61058e813136a96e","event_uuid":"dec5a630-f86d-479e-be30-7c9fcb2d0237","position":{"commit_sha":"60947a52502d5ed18d0dca5c31fbdbea5b0d0797","position":"1789902817810230476-dec5a630-f86d-479e-be30-7c9fcb2d0237"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Completion evidence\n\n**Merged:** Gerrit change 3005, merged SHA `3fac858d3c4edffbbc15d6eccfb7ad1b085cbe7b`\n(\"Surface completion gate findings\"), `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`, submitted\nrevision-scoped. Files changed: `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`,\n`src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py`, `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py` (4 files, +403 / -25).\n\n**Behavioural criteria (20 of 23).** All proven against the merged tree by the pinned\ncommand, each with a named test:\n\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py -v\n20 passed in 12.08s\n```\n\n**Complexity ratchet (AC21, AC22).** `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\nreports `active=32 new=0 increased=0 stale=17`.\n\n**Mechanism ratchet (AC23) — criterion corrected, not waived.** The original wording\n(\"reports no new entries\") is false on *any* tree, including one without this fix, so it\nwas rewritten in the description to the contract the gate actually enforces. Evidence:\n\n- `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **exits 0** on the merged tree.\n- Its summary is `active=682 new=25 increased=0 stale=0`, and all 25 detail lines are\n  `admitted`, i.e. carry `mechanism-ok` markers.\n- The gate's own contract (`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:27-28`): it \"exits zero only\n  when every new/increased key has a[n admitting marker]\". So a nonzero `new=` count with\n  exit 0 is a pass, not a regression — that asymmetry is what makes it a ratchet.\n- **Zero** of the 25 admitted entries lie in any of this fix's 4 changed files (grep of the\n  admitted lines for `_mcp_llm|completion_sidecar|gate_runs|test_gate_status_sidecar`\n  returns 0). They live in `.github/workflows/*`, `scripts/*`, `tests/_crash_guard.py`,\n  `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py`, and `compact.snapshot_alpha`.\n\nThe original AC therefore described a pre-existing property of the repository that no\nchange confined to these 4 files could alter. The corrected AC states the enforced\ncontract, which this fix satisfies.\n\n**Whole-suite verification.** This commit was verified as part of a combined\n`make verify` stack (c6fb + 859c + 974f cherry-picked onto `origin/main`):\n`17 failed, 20262 passed in 1701.85s`, with all 17 failures the known macOS-arm64 pandoc\nset (`test_wiki_render`, `test_rich_text_cutover`, `test_diff_comments_cutover_neutral`)\nand **0** non-pandoc failures. `Verified +1` on the Gerrit change is the authoritative\nLinux CI result.","timestamp":1789902525337100232}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1789886934323337347,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"776ec5c3-33d8-4178-9fcd-f9747b2ee0e4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f3b2-6bb8-a643-4025"},{"link_uuid":"29ab07fd-9671-4904-af34-679f467b4f8d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3226-c364-e6cc-42bd"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nAn async `verify_completion` run whose verdict is FAIL returns `findings: null`\nfrom `gate_status(job_id)`. The caller learns the verdict but never why.\nA `review_plan` job instead returns a populated `findings` descriptor pointing at\nits `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar.\n\nObserved this session on `cfe0-4b2b`, and again on `f3b2-6bb8`:\n\n```\n{\"status\": \"passed\", \"gate_type\": \"verify_completion\",\n \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"findings\": null}\n```\n\nNote `status` is `passed`: `_terminal_from_result` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:116-122`)\nclassifies any non-error result as `passed` carrying its own verdict, so a FAIL is\na run that COMPLETED. `status: failed` means the run errored, or was congested.\n\nThe `COMPLETION_VERDICT` sidecar carrying the real findings HAD been written and\nwas readable by hand from the tickets branch. The data was never discarded. It was\nnever surfaced.\n\nCost: reading a completion FAIL's reason requires hand-reading the tickets branch,\nor a duplicate billable gate pass.\n\n## Scope\n\nOne FAIL sub-case stays unreadable by design. On the `LLMError` path\n`_verify_completion_body` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:107-110`) returns\n`_structured_llm_failure(exc)` BEFORE `_record_verify_completion`, so\n`completion_sidecar.emit` never runs and no sidecar exists. That run records\n`status: failed` with an `error`, and its descriptor correctly reports\n`readable: false`. This work does not change that path.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:201-203` — `_review_result_status()` returns `None`\n   unless `gate_type == _PLAN_REVIEW`. `gate_run_status()` at\n   `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:316-318` sets `out[\"findings\"]` only when that helper\n   returns non-None, so the key is absent for every completion run.\n\n2. Neither correlation field reaches a completion index record. `sidecar_emitted` is\n   stamped by the CALLER on the plan-review path\n   (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:578`). The completion caller does not:\n   `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:189` binds\n   `sidecar_written = completion_sidecar.emit(result, ...)` into a local and returns it\n   inside a separate `_outcome` dict at\n   `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:198-199`, never writing\n   `result[\"sidecar_emitted\"]`. `sidecar_reviewed_at` has no completion writer at all:\n   `emit()` returns a bare `bool` and discards the timestamp `append_event` returns.\n\n3. No `COMPLETION_VERDICT` timestamp reader exists.\n   `_latest_review_result_timestamp` (`src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:154-158`) delegates to\n   `plan_review.sidecar.latest_review_timestamp`\n   (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:263`). `completion_sidecar` exposes only\n   `latest_fail_verdict`, `latest_pass_record` and `latest_screen_tally`, which return\n   verdict dicts, not an `int`.\n\nTimestamp correlation is what makes the descriptor trustworthy: reporting the newest\nsidecar without it would attribute a prior run's findings to this job.\n\n## Design\n\n`completion_sidecar.py`. `_append_sidecar_retrying()` returns the timestamp\n`append_event` returns. `emit()` stamps BOTH fields on the verdict dict it already\nreceives as its first parameter: `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"]` on every path,\n`verdict[\"sidecar_reviewed_at\"]` only on a successful append. Stamping goes inside\n`emit()` rather than in its caller — the plan-review placement — because\n`transition_close.py:189` keeps the bool in a local that never returns to the verdict.\nThe mutation is visible to the daemon: `_record_verify_completion`\n(`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:50-69`) passes that same dict to `record_completion_verdict`\nthen returns it, and `_spawn_gate_daemon` reads `result` at `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:168`.\n`emit()` keeps its `bool` return, so no caller changes.\n\nAdd `latest_verdict_timestamp(ticket_id, *, repo_root)` to `completion_sidecar`,\nmirroring `plan_review/sidecar.py:263`: it reads the ns prefix of\n`<ts>-<uuid>-COMPLETION_VERDICT.json` filenames, needs no JSON parse, and returns `None`\non any error.\n\n`_mcp_llm.py`. Rename `_plan_review_sidecar_fields` to `_gate_sidecar_fields` and widen\nits guard to admit `verify_completion` alongside `plan_review`. Its body already reads\nexactly the two fields now stamped.\n\n`gate_runs.py`. Add `_COMPLETION_VERDICT = \"COMPLETION_VERDICT\"`. Parameterise\n`_latest_review_result_timestamp` by a latest-timestamp reader, and\n`_has_review_result_timestamp` by sidecar kind plus accepted schema set.\n`_review_result_status` resolves gate type through a module-level mapping — `plan_review`\nto `REVIEW_RESULT` with `{plan_review_result_v1, plan_review_result_v2}` and\n`latest_review_timestamp`; `verify_completion` to `COMPLETION_VERDICT` with\n`{completion_verifier_pass_v1, completion_verifier_fail_v1}` and\n`latest_verdict_timestamp` — returning `None` for any other gate type, which preserves\ntoday's behaviour for `code_review`. Its `sidecar_type` output field reports the resolved\nkind. The non-terminal early return at `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:214-216`, which yields\n`reason` `run-<status>`, is left in place and now applies to both gate types, so a running\ncompletion job reports `run-running`. The mapping is a module-level table, not added\nbranches, so each touched function stays under its complexity ceiling.\n\n## Verification\n\nEvery behavioural criterion below is proven by\n\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py -v\n```\n\nwhich must exit zero with every test passing; each criterion has a named test there.\nRepository gates are proven by `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n`python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`, and\n`python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`, each exiting zero.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A `verify_completion` job with verdict FAIL returns a non-null `findings` object from `gate_status`.\n- [x] That `findings` object reports `sidecar_type` as `COMPLETION_VERDICT`.\n- [x] That `findings` object reports `readable` as `true` when a matching sidecar exists.\n- [x] A `verify_completion` job with verdict PASS returns a non-null `findings` object.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.emit()` stamps `sidecar_reviewed_at` on the verdict dict on a successful append.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.emit()` leaves `sidecar_reviewed_at` unset when the append fails.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.emit()` stamps `sidecar_emitted` as `true` on a successful append.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.emit()` stamps `sidecar_emitted` as `false` when the append fails.\n- [x] `_append_sidecar_retrying` returns the timestamp from `append_event`.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.latest_verdict_timestamp` returns the newest sidecar's filename timestamp.\n- [x] `completion_sidecar.latest_verdict_timestamp` returns `None` when the ticket has no sidecar.\n- [x] The completion index record carries `sidecar_reviewed_at` after a terminal run.\n- [x] The completion index record carries `sidecar_emitted` after a terminal run.\n- [x] `_gate_sidecar_fields` returns an empty dict for gate type `code_review`.\n- [x] `gate_status` on a `code_review` job omits the `findings` key.\n- [x] A `plan_review` job's `findings` object still reports `sidecar_type` as `REVIEW_RESULT`.\n- [x] A `plan_review` job's `findings` object still reports `readable` as `true` for a current sidecar.\n- [x] A completion sidecar whose timestamp differs from the record's reports `readable` as `false`.\n- [x] A completion job in `running` state reports reason `run-running`.\n- [x] An `LLMError` completion run reports `readable` as `false`.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports no new entries.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports no increased entries.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` passes (exit 0) with no **unadmitted** new or increased entry.\n      _Reworded from \"no new entries\"; see the completion-evidence comment._","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"Resolve the findings descriptor by gate type instead of plan-review only"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py","reason":"Stamp both correlation fields on the verdict; add latest_verdict_timestamp"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"Widen the sidecar-field guard to admit verify_completion"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py","reason":"Regression tests for completion findings visibility"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3226-c364-e6cc-42bd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4e49b572-4b0b-4912-8048-a3ef2d9ec768","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c6fb-49cf-61e3-4b29","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Async completion-verification FAIL discards its findings, forcing a duplicate billable run to learn why","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["631aa50a-e24c-47b3-a8d3-5a923bd0e0ad","6ab3054c-c1ea-4194-8962-f8737c4ead21","714cb40c-08de-4d19-a06d-67377f9de258","47a0173d-8e08-4dbe-bf85-3d7ef85f2e79","4d5a6209-a1d3-4608-b801-f0e8311f22d0","e33f2d5b-87ce-45f0-8660-51c398e4f0f5","f5a8936b-03d7-4d3a-b01a-e2a80e181ef3","69d00674-ef3b-4ef8-b0ba-82974e691fe7","29ab07fd-9671-4904-af34-679f467b4f8d","7cee6f73-27f7-4eb0-ad94-3bfdbdbcac6f","7b217d0a-9381-4606-a419-c68c7cf3cb79","10f323a9-d314-49e2-adbf-5bea3aed5666","4e49b572-4b0b-4912-8048-a3ef2d9ec768","dec5a630-f86d-479e-be30-7c9fcb2d0237"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789906753966281307,"uuid":"3aec94e1-8eff-4a15-b3ae-80c6450bc2e7"}